# pony staging collision — found and fixed by worker 162 (2026-10-09)

## Finding

`stage_pinned.py` (156's S1) staged raw downloads at
`raw / sid / Path(f["path"]).name` — the bare basename. For
bright-pony BOTH files share the basename
`pony-00000-of-00001.parquet` (`documents/...` = corpus,
1,125,040 B; `examples/...` = queries_and_gold, 27,722 B), so
the second fetch overwrote the first. The source record then
listed BOTH roles against the same local path (examples bytes),
and the TB-cache placement copied examples bytes into BOTH
`bright/raw/documents/` and `bright/raw/examples/`.

Proven on VM 2026-10-09:
- `tb-cache/bright/raw/documents/pony-*.parquet`:
  27,722 B, sha256 `0c0718d3…` = examples bytes, NOT the
  pinned corpus bytes (1,125,040 B, `afc23dc0…`).
- 162 re-verify of `_pinned_raw` against the source record:
  7/8 OK; `bright-pony:documents/...` MISMATCH (on-disk file
  was examples bytes).

## Consequence for SCOPE §8

SCOPE §8 ("bright-pony DROPPED") diagnosed the pinned corpus
file as holding the 112-row examples table — but that
diagnosis was made on COLLIDED bytes (the staged documents/
copy was examples bytes, hence `KeyError: 'content'`).
The TRUE pinned corpus bytes (re-fetched 2026-10-09 from the
same pinned URL, 1,125,040 B, sha256 `afc23dc0…` verified)
contain a VALID document pool: 7,894 rows, columns
`id`/`content` — exactly the SCOPE §4 expectation
(7,894 docs / 112 queries).

The drop cause was a staging bug, not an upstream defect.
Pony is recoverable WITHIN the pinned-links requirement
(same commit `3066d29c…`, same bytes, hash-verified), so 162
recovered the lane instead of honoring a mistaken drop. No
upstream substitution of any kind.

## Fix (162)

`adapters/stage_pinned.py`: raw dest is now
`raw / sid / f["path"]` (mirrors upstream repo layout;
role dirs disambiguate colliding basenames).
- Local sha before: `dfa113b8…`; after: `06b279cd…`
  (`py_compile` PASS).
- Transited to VM via GCS
  (`gs://tl-m2-runs-d1995b06/m2/lane-bench10m/code/
  stage_pinned-162.py`), sha re-verified on arrival.
- 156's original preserved at `/tmp/stage_pinned-156-orig.py`
  on the VM (not in the lane tree; reference only).

## Restage (162, fixed script, `--cache tb-cache`)

- Same vendor manifest (`upstream-links.json` sha
  `e5fb424a…` = local manifest sha).
- BEIR jsonl byte-identical to 156's (pre/post restage shas):
  scifact corpus `f4a47c54…`, queries `154a7577…`;
  nfcorpus corpus `23387b39…`, queries `b248055b…`.
  Counts identical (5183/1109/339/300; 3633/3237/12334/323).
  156's `prepared/` + completed BEIR/curated/smoke RUNs are
  therefore unaffected (inputs provably unchanged).
- Pony documents now stage the true corpus bytes
  (`afc23dc0…`, 1,125,040 B); `setup --dataset bright-pony`
  froze `prepared/bright-pony/test/` (112 cases, 7,894 docs).
- Collided stray `_pinned_raw/bright-pony/pony-*.parquet`
  removed after replacement (recorded here).
- `--cross-check-ukp` NOT re-run (156's record stands:
  docs+queries identical, qrels bytes differ); restage
  byte-identity above subsumes it.

## Lesson for larger rungs (also in REPORT.md)

Stage raw files under role-qualified paths (done), and
schema-check every staged corpus file (row counts + required
columns) BEFORE setup — the check SCOPE §8 recommended would
have caught this at staging time.
